  "intro": [
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "tone": "info",
      "text": "**How to use this template**\n1. Copy `template/tds/v1.json` to `<project>/tds/v1.json` and set `prdVersion` to the PRD version it's written against.\n2. Keep the section numbers. Write \"N/A — [reason]\" in a section rather than deleting it, so reviewers can see it was considered. Validation fails on a missing or empty section.\n3. Items marked 🔒 **Mandated** are the Scentia standard. A project may deviate from one only with an ADR (section 17) approved by Matt Stejer.\n4. Items marked ✏️ are project-specific: fill them in.\n5. Delete the 💡 guidance callouts once a section is complete.\n6. Diagrams are Mermaid blocks (section 3.1), so they can be diffed, copied and reviewed as text.\n7. The TDS describes *how* the system is built. Behaviour lives in the user stories and the repo's `docs/SPEC.md`: link to them rather than restating them.\n8. Every change is a new version: copy the latest file to the next number (v2.json, v3.json…) and update its version header. Merged versions never change, and CI fails if one does.\n9. Worked example: the Partner Packs Portal TDS (`partner-pack-portals/tds/v1.json`)."
    }
  ],
