    {
      "number": "7",
      "title": "Integrations",
      "blocks": [],
      "subsections": [
        {
          "number": "7.1",
          "title": "Integration standards",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "🔒 Every integration must have:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "**Inbound webhooks:** signature verification, replay protection (timestamp window), Zod validation, idempotent processing keyed on the provider's event ID, and a 2xx response only after the event is durably recorded.",
                "**Outbound writes:** sent through a Queue with an idempotency key, exponential backoff, a dead-letter queue, and an alert when anything lands in the DLQ.",
                "**Reconciliation:** a scheduled job that compares state and reports drift, for any data held on both sides.",
                "**Failure visibility:** failed syncs are visible to internal users in the app, not only in logs.",
                "**Least-privilege credentials:** a dedicated integration user or API key per environment, scoped to the minimum objects and actions."
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "number": "7.2",
          "title": "Integration catalogue",
          "blocks": [
